# GitHub reads this file and shows "Cite this repository" in the sidebar (docs: About CITATION files).
# No `version:` and no `date-released:` on purpose: the version has one home, krokai/__init__.py,
# and a second copy here would go stale on the next release (selftest suite_docs checks both keys
# are absent).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KrokAI Law in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "KrokAI Law (krokai): AI citation and quote checker for legal documents"
abstract: >-
  A free, open-source command-line tool that checks every quotation in a legal
  document drafted with AI word for word against the statutes, regulations,
  USCIS Policy Manual chapters and case law kept on your own disk. It runs
  offline, and no AI model decides the verdict.
authors:
  - family-names: Saevets
    given-names: Igor
repository-code: "https://github.com/igorsaevets/krokai-law"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/krokai/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - legal citation checker
  - quotation verification
  - AI hallucination
  - legal tech
  - USCIS
  - immigration law
  - EB-2 NIW
  - EB-1A
